cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use llmledger, please cite it as below."
title: "llmledger: what happens to an LLM after it joins a price catalogue"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Emami Tabrizi"
    given-names: "Pouria"
version: 1.16.0
date-released: 2026-10-19
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23330454
repository-code: "https://github.com/pouriaetab/llmledger"
url: "https://pouriaetab.github.io/llmledger/"
abstract: >-
  Rebuilds the full git history of LiteLLM's model price file and estimates,
  with competing risks survival analysis (Aalen-Johansen with bootstrap
  intervals), how likely a newly added model is to have its price changed,
  get a retirement date, or be removed. Results are republished daily, with a
  lookup for every model, a cost calculator for text, images, video and speech,
  a best value finder using Arena ratings with an automatic task guess,
  a replay of Arena's past leaderboards with the price of top quality over time,
  flags for corrections and bulk
  clean ups, and an independent SQL cross-check.
keywords:
  - survival analysis
  - competing risks
  - Aalen-Johansen
  - LLM pricing
  - LiteLLM
